## main.py: Qt App Initialisation

For `QMetaObject` and signals to work, a `QApplication` instance must
exist on the main thread before any Qt objects are created.
Add to `main.py` before supervisor starts:

```python
from PyQt5.QtWidgets import QApplication
import sys

qt_app = QApplication.instance() or QApplication(sys.argv)
```

The main thread loop changes to:

```python
try:
    while state.is_running():
        qt_app.processEvents()
        time.sleep(0.05)
except KeyboardInterrupt:
    ...
```

This keeps the Qt event loop ticking on the main thread so signals
delivered to it are processed.

