## Tray Class

```python
class TrayApp:
    def __init__(self, state: AppState, config: dict)
    def build_menu(self) -> pystray.Menu
    def start(self) -> None      # blocking — runs pystray loop
    def stop(self) -> None       # called from outside to stop tray
```

`start()` calls `pystray.Icon.run()` which blocks.
It must run in its own thread so `main.py` is not blocked.

